{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Behold.</b> מְסַעֵף — He will cut off the branches, like לֹא תְפָאֵר אַחֲרֶיךָ (Deuteronomy 24:20) and וְשָׁרֶשְׁךָ מֵאֶרֶץ חַיִּים (Psalms 52:7):" "<b>Its glory.</b> Like branch, and similarly וְתִשְׁלַח פֹּארֹת (Ezekiel 17:6):" "<b>With terrifying power.</b> With might, from the root of עָרִיץ:" "<b>And those of lofty stature.</b> Because the princes have been cut off:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:22.887708879Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}